{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-30T13:54:31.173Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7b0e58428f53e3aaeaafb372","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.312","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-stq61b"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Unknown-option recovery drops a dash-leading prose value: the advertised replay closes, comments or creates without the user's text"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found while closing pm-gh1633. Its close reason began with '--unset', and pm close <id> \"--unset accepts ...\" was refused as unknown option '--unset accepts ...'. Commander treats any argv token that starts with '--' as an option, even a quoted multi-word value. The generic unknown-option fallback in resolveUnknownOptionRetry then removes that token and advertises the remainder as 'Replay with suggested correction'. Reproduced on this branch in an isolated tracker:\n\n- pm close <id> \"--unset is now a list\" suggests pm close <id>, which closes with no reason.\n- pm comments <id> \"--flag style comment text\" suggests pm item comments <id>, which drops the comment.\n- pm create \"--weird title\" --type Task suggests pm create --type Task, which drops the title.\n\nThe refusal also calls the prose 'not declared on any command path' and advises a nearest option. A token containing whitespace can never be an option spelling, and pm close <id> -- \"--unset is now a list\" works today. Replaying the advertised command loses user data or performs a different mutation, which breaks the recovery contract that a suggested retry preserves intent."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","recovery","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-30T13:54:31.173Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-30T13:54:31.173Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Never advertise a retry that drops a whitespace-bearing unknown-option token; Offer a -- separator retry only when it preserves the value and all other arguments in order; Explain in the refusal that the value starts with -- and how to pass it, without the declared-nowhere option advice; Cover close, comments and create through SDK and CLI tests, with a pre-fix negative control"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A dash-leading prose value is never dropped by an advertised replay; when safe, the replay passes it after a -- separator, otherwise the refusal explains how to pass it."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"cli"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-fo8g7j","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-30T13:54:31.173Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1633","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-10-30T13:54:31.173Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-p316vn","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-30T13:54:31.173Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-30T13:54:31.173Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Duplicate check: a semantic search for an unknown-option fallback dropping positional dash-leading text, and a keyword search for 'suggested_retry drops'. The nearest closed owners are pm-p316vn (close retry preserves named options), pm-fo8g7j (refusal identifies the actual rejected flag) and pm-8nyc/pm-in23qu (suggestion quality). None covers a whitespace-bearing token being parsed as an option and then deleted from the replay, so this is a distinct boundary."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"28ec6b0d77ad802d8b3fc2eecd99c35fd496f002cbfbeab10c2abff75a579c76","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1e4592790f8953727ee8faa1f2529793af16acad447f3339ebf6f3588ff80849"}
